2 CONC  1886, 417; Introduction It is very doubtful whether the Danish Barfods belong to the Pomeranian / Brandenburg family Barfus - they use a different weapon! '''Albrecht and his son Marquard are 1453, 1454 and 1461, and their seals 
2 CONC show 2 full + 2 half footprints with their toes upwards, placed in a sloping beam (Marquard in the left-hand slope)'''. In the recipe of the sails '''they write Bareffoet or Barfod'''. A.This: Danish Adele Sigiller from the 15 '16
2 CONC ' and 17 'Century. 1905. '''The name Barfus is not seen in Denmark at all'''. Source: Denmark's Old Personal Names. The connection to Pomerania / Brandenburg is then similar to a family book fief fantasy.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''There is no evidence to call the genus Barfus'''. Now we have another genus Barfod that was adorned 1455, so confusion we can easily make. I will then call the families: Barfod [ff Barfus] and Barfod [of 1455]. All treated I ha
2 CONC ve been through all the people of the family. All 3. Pedigree S 58 (without number, ancestor) '''Albrecht Barfod''' [ff Barfus] (-1434-1459-) to Alsted 1432 seals a 'Barfod' for Torkil Perssen (Weapons) in Føvling (now: Våbensholm
2 CONC ). It must be Albrecht, which is only 10 km mlm Alsted and Våbensholm. Source: Repertory - Danm.'s Letters from the Middle Ages. 1432 No. 6563.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is already seen in 1434 to Alsted, and yet 1459. Source: Staircase: Denmark. Bd 21 Vejle a, p 1056: Alsted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Named 1434, 1440, 1440, 1440, 1444, 1446, 1452, 1453, 1453, 1454, 1468. Source: Denmark's old personal names. 1949-53.
2 CONT
2 CONT Named 1459 as one of the heirs of Ribe Dean Anders Skeel. Source: DAA 1943: Skeel. S 94 No. 13. S 58 (without number) '''Anne Albrechtsdatter Barfod''' [ff Barfus] (-1508-) Gm Erik Vestenie (-1467-1506-) to Søbygård and Refstrup T
2 CONC hey gave (both) 1508 into Randers Holy Spirit House. In the Vestenie board it is only her, and she first establishes a soul mate. Erik is seen last time 1506. Source: DAA 1932: Vestenie. S 185.
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik is written to Sæbygaard. It is Søbygård in Søby s, Gjern hrd. It is known not to be called Sæbygård. Source: Staircase: Denmark. Bd 22 Skanderbg, 581: Søbygård. Correction 1886: '''Marquard Barfod''' [Former Barfus] (-1461-) 
