1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_V_of_Denmark '''Eric V Klipping'''] was King of Denmark (1259–1286) and son of King Christopher I of Denmark. From 1259-1266, he ruled under the auspices of his competent mother,
2 CONC  Margaret Sambiria (1230-1282). Between 1261 and 1262, the young King Eric was a prisoner in Holstein following a military defeat. Afterwards, he lived in Brandenburg, where he was initially held captive by John I, Margrave of Bra
2 CONC ndenburg (c. 1213-1266) 
