1 NOTE By her marriage to Valdemar IV Atterdag (1340-75), her father gave her 1/4 of Jutland as dowry which he had in security for lones to the Danish kings and other royals who had engaged in a long civil war. Most of the country was in
2 CONC  the hands of the Holstein Counts, but her dowry was a contributing factor to the fact that her husband managed to win back all the territory - giving him his by-name "Day again". Helvig must have acted as regent during her husban
2 CONC d's many journeys abroad, but she also seems to have ended her day's in a convent. She was the mother of Margrethe I of Denmark, and died (ca. 1374).
