1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She also had royal blood in her veins, and she also descended from Marsk Stig.
2 CONT
2 CONT The result was that Axel Jepsen's brother-in-law, ridder and rigsråd Jacob Andersen Bjørn got the farm. He was a great estate-collector. When he married Margrethe Poulsdatter (Fikkesen?), he got as a dowry Tybjerggård, and he was 
2 CONC the owner of Vorgård in Himmerland. And also Støvringgård after his marriage. After his death fru Margrethe managed his estates for many years, but she lived mostly at Støvringgård. From two children her son Anders died unmarried 
2 CONC in 1536. The daughter Dorte was married twice, first time to Christopher Hak of Egholm and second time to Oluf Glob of Vellumgård, but there were no children in either marriage, and the estates went after her death ab.1562 to her 
2 CONC cousin Anne Bjørnsdatter's children. Fru Anne was married to Niels Kaas of Stårupgård and Tårupgård, and two of their sons, Niels and Erik Kaas, inherited Støvringgård.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:TcyNVRQMSf0J:www.djoef-forlag.dk/media/21ecdd44-8dc3-40c9-9463-f3e6cff5e6de/Downloads/9788757401622/domme1_htm+&cd=3&hl=en&ct=clnk&gl=dk] DJOEF: Nr. 132 • Viborg 05.05.1537 Dom
2 CONC bog 1, Fol. 50R-50V Glob Krabbe; Ib (adelig; gejstlig • Østergård, Åsted S., Harre H., Viborg A.; Højslev S. & By, Fjends H., Viborg A.) mod Anne Bjørnsdatter (adel • Stårupgård, Højslev S., Fjends H., Viborg A.) Hævd og besiddels
2 CONC e - jordegods (ejendom, enge, marker) • Kongen fraværende; 19 fraværende fra rådet • 1. instans. Udfald: Frikendelse Resume: Sagsøgerne tiltalte sagsøgte ang. ejendomsretten til nogle enge og jord.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thyrashm.blogspot.dk/2010/05/stvringgard-east-jutland-randers-amt.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Datteren Anne blev gift med Niels Kaas paa Staarupgaard og fik med ham 10 børn, bl.a. Jens (f. 1516), Bjørn og Niels (f. 1534), den senere kansler. De var altsaa fætre til Bjørn Andersen, og det var gennem moderen, at sønnerne fra
2 CONC  Staarupgaard senere arvede Vorgård og Støvringgaard.
