1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Laurids Lindenov was a war commissary during the Scanian War (Skånska kriget) 1676-1679 and worked mainly in the Kristianstad area in northeastern Scania. Several of his reports from the war are preserved in the Na
2 CONC tional Archives in Copenhagen. He worked closely with the local irregular troops known as the friskytter or snaphaner and passed on reports from them to Commander-in-Chief Friedrich von Arenstorff. 
2 CONT After the war, he became county governor (amtmand) in Bergenhus County in Norwary.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://skeel.info/getperson.php?personID=I9257&tree=ks
