2 CONT
2 CONT Kirsten Madsdatter (died 1613) was King Christian IV of Denmark's lover, and the mother of one of his three acknowledged, illegitimate sons, Christian Ulrik Gyldenløve.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kirsten Madsdatter was likely the daughter of Copenhagen's mayor Mathias Hansen, though this is unconfirmed. She was originally a chambermaid to Queen Anna Catherine. The relationship started before the death of the queen; their s
2 CONC on was born in 1611. In 1612, the queen died. In 1613, Kirsten died and was replaced by Karen Andersdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathias_Hansen_House]
2 CONT
