3 CONT
3 CONT
3 CONT Anne of Denmark (1574-1619) was queen consort of Scotland, England, and Ireland as the wife of King James VI and I.
3 CONT She was the daughter of King Frederick II of Denmark, and at the age of fourteen she married James in 1589. She
3 CONT bore him three children who survived infancy, including the future Charles I. In England, Anne shifted her energies
3 CONT from factional politics to patronage of the arts and constructed a magnificent court of her own, hosting one of the richest
3 CONT cultural salons in Europe.
3 CONT
3 CONT from:  http://polarbearstale.blogspot.com/2010/10/anne-of-denmark-1574-1619.html
