1 OCCU Markgraf von Brandenburg
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Heinrich I Margrave of Brandenburg-Stendal, "ohne Land"=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Markgraf Johann von Brandenburg, I and Markgrafin Brigitte von Sachsen, Markgräfin von Brandenburg 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRANDENBURG,%20PRUSSIA.htm#JohannIdied12661267 Project MedLands, Prussia, Brandenburg]
2 CONT
2 CONT HEINRICH [I] von Brandenburg "ohne Land" (1260-14 Feb 1318). The Cronica Principum Saxonie names (in order) "Albertum, Hermannum et Henricum" as sons of "Iohannes" and his second wife Jutta[336]. The Annales Lubicenses names "Agne
2 CONC tem filiam marchionis de Brandenborch, sororis Ottonis marchionis cum thelo et Hinrici marchionis dicti ane land"[337]. "Otto…Brandenburg et de Landesberg marchio" granted Schloß Querfurt to the bishop of Brandenburg, with the con
2 CONC sent of "fratris nostri Hinrici…patruelium nostrorum Johannis et Wolmari, de Brandenburg et de Landesberg Marchionum", by charter dated 10 Jan 1305[338]. m ([Nov 1298/19 May 1303], Papal dispensation Anagni 19 May 1303) as her sec
2 CONC ond husband, AGNES von Bayern, widow of HEINRICH Landgraf von Hessen, daughter of LUDWIG II "der Strenge" Duke of Bavaria, Pfalzgraf bei Rhein & his third wife Mechtild von Habsburg ([1276/78]-22 Jul 1345). Her origin is confirmed
2 CONC  by the charter dated 21 Aug 1323 under which "Ludowicus…Romanorum Rex" granted rights to "Sophie…sororis nostre Agnetis, relicte quondam Henrici Marchionis Brandenburgensis, filie"[339]. Burchard Archbishop of Magdeburg agreed an
2 CONC  alliance with “Agn der Margreuinen von Brandenborch unde tu Landesberch”, with the consent of “hertoghen Hinrike von Brunswik erem swaghere”, by charter dated 16 Apr 1318[340]. Markgraf Heinrich & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1) '''''JUTTA''''' ([1299/1306]-[15 Jul 1325/early Feb 1327]). Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the charter dated 16 Apr 1318 under which Burchard Archbishop of Magdeburg agreed an alliance with “Agn der Margreuinen v
2 CONC on Brandenborch unde tu Landesberch” with the consent of “hertoghen Hinrike von Brunswik erem swaghere”[341]. m (before 16 Apr 1318) as his first wife, HEINRICH von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen, son of HEINRICH I Herzog von Braunschwe
2 CONC ig und Lüneburg in Grubenhagen und Salzderhelden & his wife Agnes von Meissen ([1289]-[10 Apr/8 Jun] 1351, bur Grubenhagen). He succeeded his father in 1322 as HEINRICH II "der Junge" Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2) '''''SOPHIE''''' (1300-[1356]). "Ludowicus…Romanorum Rex" granted rights to "Sophie…sororis nostre Agnetis, relicte quondam Henrici Marchionis Brandenburgensis, filie" by charter dated 21 Aug 1323[342]. m MAGNUS I Herzog von 
2 CONC Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Göttingen, son of ALBRECHT II "der Fette/der Feiste" Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Göttingen und Braunschweig & his wife Richza von Werle ([1304]-[15 Jun/15 Aug] 1369, bur Lüneburg St Michael
2 CONC is). 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3) '''''MARGARETE''''' (1301-31 Mar 1347, bur Weissenfels St Klara). Abbess of St Klara at Weissenfels.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 4)  '''''HEINRICH von Brandenburg''''' ([1302/10]-early Jul 1320, bur Prenzlau Marienkirche). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry I, Markgraf von Brandenburg is Queen Elizabeth II's 15th great grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margrave Henry I (nicknamed Henry Lackland; 21 March 1256 – 14 February 1318) was a member of the House of Ascania and Margrave of Brandenburg-Stendal and Landsberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry I, Margrave of Brandenburg-Stendal
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry I and Otto IV
2 CONT
2 CONT Born:	21 March 1256
2 CONT
2 CONT Died:	14 February 1318 (aged 61)
2 CONT
2 CONT Noble family:	House of Ascania
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse(s):	Agnes of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Father:	John I, Margrave of Brandenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother:	Jutta of Saxony
2 CONT
2 CONT Margrave Henry I (nicknamed Henry Lackland; 21 March 1256 – 14 February 1318) was a member of the House of Ascania and Margrave of Brandenburg-Stendal and Landsberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriage and issue==
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was married to Agnes, the daughter of Duke Louis II "the Strict" of Bavaria and widow of Landgrave Henry the Younger of Hesse. Henry and Agnes had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Henry II, Margrave of Brandenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT *Sophia (1300-1356), married Duke Magnus I of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel
2 CONT
2 CONT *Judith, married in 1318 to Duke Henry II of Brunswick-Grubenhagen
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_I,_Margrave_of_Brandenburg-Stendal Wikipedia Henry I Margrave of Brandenburg]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Life==
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was a son of Margrave John I of Brandenburg and his third wife, Jutta, the daughter of Duke Albert I of Saxony. The origin of his nickname "Lackland" is not known. Henry was more than fifteen years younger than his brothers 
2 CONC John II, Otto IV "with the arrow" and Conrad I and was therefore likely to be excluded from governing when his brothers inherited the Margraviate.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was not until 1294 he began to participate in the government of the country. When he did, he received — according to an excerpt from the Bohemian chronicler Přibík Pulkava — Delitzsch as his seat. Delitzsch was located in the M
2 CONC argraviate of Landsberg, which Margrave Albert II of Meissen had sold to the Margraves of Brandenburg. From then on, Henry used the title of Margrave of Landsberg in addition to Margrave of Brandenburg in almost all documents. As 
2 CONC Margrave of Landsberg, he fought several feuds with neighbouring princes. He was excommunicated by archbishop Burchard II of Magdeburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1311, Henry lost a feud to Duke Rudolf I of Saxony and had to hand over the County Palatine of Saxony with the castles Grillenberg Castle in Sangerhausen and Raspenburg Castle in Rastenberg to Rudolf I. He also lost a feud to M
2 CONC argrave Dietrich IV of Lusatia.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Emperor Henry VII, Henry's nephew Margrave Waldemar proposed to elect Henry I as King of the Romans. Henry I appears to have declined the proposal, and his promised by deed to vote for Duke Frederick the Fair or his brother 
2 CONC Leopold I. However, in the end, Henry voted for Duke Louis IV of Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry died on 14 February 1318 at the age of 61 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''The Peerage'''''' - http://thepeerage.com/p534.htm#i5333
2 CONT
