1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/DUTCH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc457229112 v3.5 Updated 07 November 2016
2 CONT
2 CONT GIJSBRECHT [II] van Bronkhorst (-after 12 Sep 1237).  Heer van Bronkhorst.  “...Domini Giselberti de Brunkhurst...” witnessed the charter dated 11 Jun 1231 under which Otto Graaf van Gelre granted freedoms to “civitati de Herderew
2 CONC ich”[366].  “Giselbertum nobilem de Brunchorst...et uxor mea Conegundis” settled a dispute with “capitulum Sutphaniensis ecclesie” concerning “decima...ab antiqua insula Brunckhorst usque Nierstat” by charter dated 10 Sep 1232, wi
2 CONC tnessed by “...Henricus clericus frater ipsius nobilis de Brunchorst...”[367].  “Nobilium meorum...Gyselbertus de Bronckhorst...” witnessed the charter dated 15 Jul 1233 under which Otto Graaf van Gelre granted rights to “Arnhem c
2 CONC ivitatem”[368].  “Giselbertus miles de Brunchorst...et uxor mea Kunegundis” exchanged “decimam trium domorum in parrochia Vurden” with Klooster Bethlehem for “Venewic...in parrochia Stenre” by charter dated 23 Nov 1235, witnessed 
2 CONC by “...Henrico fratre meo Sutphaniense canonico...”[369].  “...Dominus Gysekinus de Brunchurst...” witnessed the charter dated 12 Sep 1237 under which Otto Graaf van Gelre granted freedoms to “opido nostro...Doseburg”[370].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m as her second husband, KUNIGUNDE von Oldenburg, widow of --- von Ahaus, daughter of MORITZ Graf von Oldenburg & his wife Salome von Wickrath (-1264 or after).  Her parentage and two marriages are shown in Europäische Stammtafeln
2 CONC  but the primary source on which this information is based has not been identified[371].  “Giselbertum nobilem de Brunchorst...et uxor mea Conegundis” settled a dispute with “capitulum Sutphaniensis ecclesie” concerning “decima...
2 CONC ab antiqua insula Brunckhorst usque Nierstat” by charter dated 10 Sep 1232, witnessed by “...Henricus clericus frater ipsius nobilis de Brunchorst...”[372].  “Giselbertus miles de Brunchorst...et uxor mea Kunegundis” exchanged “de
2 CONC cimam trium domorum in parrochia Vurden” with Klooster Bethlehem for “Venewic...in parrochia Stenre” by charter dated 23 Nov 1235, witnessed by “...Henrico fratre meo Sutphaniense canonico...”[373]. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gijsbert_III_van_Bronckhorst
