2 CONT
2 CONT Moritz [I] & his wife had six children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT d) '''KUNIGUNDE von Oldenburg''' (-1264 or after).  “Comes Mauritius de Aldenburg” sold property to Kloster Bassum, when “filiam meam parvulam Salome” entered the monastery, with the consent of “uxore mea Salome et filiis...Christ
2 CONC iano et Ottone...et filiabus meis Hathewige, Cunigunde, Salome et Oda”, by charter dated to before 1209[53].  “Giselbertum nobilem de Brunchorst...et uxor mea Conegundis” settled a dispute with “capitulum Sutphaniensis ecclesie” c
2 CONC oncerning “decima...ab antiqua insula Brunckhorst usque Nierstat” by charter dated 10 Sep 1232, witnessed by “...Henricus clericus frater ipsius nobilis de Brunchorst...”[54].  “Giselbertus miles de Brunchorst...et uxor mea Kunegu
2 CONC ndis” exchanged “decimam trium domorum in parrochia Vurden” with Klooster Bethlehem for “Venewic...in parrochia Stenre” by charter dated 23 Nov 1235, witnessed by “...Henrico fratre meo Sutphaniense canonico...”[55].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly --- von Ahaus, son of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly GIJSBRECHT [II] Heer van Bronkhorst, son of --- (-after 12 Sep 1237). 
