1 OCCU Lågfrälse fogde på slottet Tre Kronor, domare, Väpnare, fogde på slottet Tre Kronor, Häradshövding i Frötuna skeppslag, Fogde och svenskt riksråd på Slottet
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nils_Kettilsson_(Vasa)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Nils Kettilsson (Vasa)=
2 CONT
2 CONT *Son of Kettil 
2 CONT * King Albrecht's adviser and official at Stockholm Castle in 1354 and 1355.
2 CONT * The oldest well-educated member of the family is Nils Kettilsson (Vaasa) (died earliest 1378) who is mentioned for the first time in 1355 . [ 16 ] and first as an adult mentioned as a gunsmith , bailiff at the castle Tre Kronor 
2 CONC during the 1350s, and 1367 district chief in Frötuna shipyard in Roslagen.
2 CONT * During the revolt against Magnus Eriksson , which led to Albrekt of Mecklenburg becoming king of Sweden, Nils Kettilsson supported the Mecklenburg duke Albrekt, at least since his troops won in Sweden, and he married Christina J
2 CONC onsdotter (Rickebyätten) ( Kristiern from Ölands ) no later than 1369 grandson's daughter) which gave him entry into the Swedish nobility. Nils Kettilsson used a coat of arms similar to the Scherembekes family.
2 CONT * Nils Kettilsson had the daughters Ramborg, married to Tord Bonde , and Ingeborg, a nun in Sankta Klara kloster and possibly identical with an abbess there, and their son Kristiern. [ 17 ]
2 CONT * [http://runeberg.org/nfck/0401.html '''The Vase, Swedish genealogy, finally royal dynasty in Sweden and Poland.''']  Already in the 13th century there were three special lineages in the Roslagen with the shield mark, which from 
2 CONC Gustaf I's time due to a gradually changed form was called "the vase". The fact that they were interrelated and constituted branches of the same tribe is for many reasons very likely. Two of them were extinct already during the Mi
2 CONC ddle Ages, without actually having succeeded in raising themselves out of the provincial low nobility class. The third, on the other hand, seems to  have belonged to lower salvation at first , but it was counted from the last half
2 CONC  of the 15th century to the country's foremost high-ranking families. Its first, historically certified member was the gunner Nils Kettilsson, who is mentioned in 1361-78 (see V. 1). A son to him was the Grand Master Kristiern Nil
2 CONC sson (see V. 2), among whose sons and grandsons several took up a marked political position during the Middle Ages (see V. 3-9).  -
2 CONT * [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vasa,_Skepptuna '''The name Vasa for the royal branch of this family, has origin in the Estate Wasa, known and documented under this name since it was owned by Nils Kettilsson.''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000000735972498&photo_id=6000000176449594887&position=0 '''Vasa’s Family Coat of Arms''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Vasa#TAB_8 Royal Family of Vaasa]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Kettilsson to Björnö , † after 1378. Lordship in Frötuna. (black straw vase in yellow field). King bailiff and official at Stockholm Castle in 1354 and 1355. In 1371 and 1376 he was called King Albrecht's adviser in Sweden. '
2 CONC ''Married before 1369 with Cristina Jonsdotter,''' † after 1378. Daughter of the knight Jon Nilsson Rickebyätten (seven-edged white star in blue and red field) and Märta Båth who was the daughter of Sune Joensson to Flishult .
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ramborg Nilsdotter,''' married before 1376 with the knight and the national council Tord Röriksson Bonde , † 1417-03-21 and buried in Vadstena monastery. Grandmother to King Karl Knutsson Farmer .
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Nilsdotter,''' Nun in St. Klara Kloster / A.
2 CONT * '''Christiern Nilsson,''' born 1365, died 1442-04-29 at Viborg Castle and was buried so. June 29 in Stockholm's gray brothers convent. Chief white man at Viborg. Knights, national council and drots. Married 1st with Margareta Jo
2 CONC hansdotter , † in Uppsala and buried 1413-08-07 in Vadstena monastery. Daughter of the knight Johan Moltke and Katarina Glysingsdotter . Married 2nd: 1426 to Margareta Eriksdotter born 1390, † 1451-06-09 and was buried in Gråbrödr
2 CONC aklostret in Stockholm, in her 2nd marriage . Her 1st marriage to Ture Stensson Bielke . Daughter of the Danish National Council Erik Krummedigeand Beata von Thienen 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source'''  Vasa Nobility 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=+10865&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Eftermedelt
