1 CONT Anne Oldenburg, Princess of Denmark was the daughter of Frederik II Oldenburg, King of Denmark <p10139.htm> and Sophia von Mecklenburg-Güstrow <p10139.htm>. She was born on 14 October 1574 at Skanderborg Castle, Jylland, Denmark.1
1 CONC  She married James I Charles Stuart, King of Great Britain <p10137.htm>, son of Henry Stuart, Lord Darnley <p10190.htm> and Mary Stewart, Queen of Scotland <p10189.htm>, on 23 November 1589 at Oslo, Norway, in a, and again on 21 J
1 CONC an 1590 at Kronberg Castle, Copenhagen, Denmark marriage.1 She died on 4 March 1619 at age 44 at Hampton Court Palace, Kingston-upon-Thames, London, England.1 She was buried at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.1  Sh
1 CONC e gained the title of Princess Anne of Denmark on 14 October 1574. Through her marriage, Anne Oldenburg, Princess of Denmark gained the title of Queen Consort Anne of Scotland on 17 May 1590.1 Through her marriage, Anne Oldenburg,
1 CONC  Princess of Denmark gained the title of Queen Consort Anne of Great Britain on 25 July 1603.1 She was godmother for Henry Stuart, 8th Seigneur d'Aubigny <p529.htm> at his baptism on 2 April 1616 at Chapel Royal, Whitehall, London
1 CONC , England.2
1 CONT Children of Anne Oldenburg, Princess of Denmark and James I Charles Stuart, King of Great Britain <p10137.htm>:
1 CONT Henry Frederick Stuart, Prince of Wales b. 19 Feb 1594, d. 6 Nov 1612 child Stuart <p10502.htm> b. Jul 1595, d. Jul 1595 Elizabeth Stuart, Princess of England+ b. 19 Aug 1596, d. 13 Feb 1662 Margaret Stuart b. 24 Dec 1598, d. Mar 
1 CONC 1600 Charles I Stuart, King of Great Britain+ b. 19 Nov 1600, d. 30 Jan 1649 Robert Bruce Stuart, Duke of Kintyre b. 18 Jan 1602, d. 27 May 1602 Son Stuart b. May 1603, d. May 1603 Mary Stuart b. 8 Apr 1605, d. 16 Sep 1607 Sophia 
1 CONC Stuart b. 22 Jun 1606, d. 23 Jun 1606
1 CONT Citations
